        "created_at": "2018-05-31T11:37:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Okay, so I’m sure several, if not all of you, have the foil cards. And I’m assuming most of you are eagle eyed. So, I was wondering if you noticed a peculiar thing about Mr. Fixer’s incap, both foil and regular.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here’s mr. fixer’s incap</p><p><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span></p><p>And here’s his foil incap</p><p><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span></p><p>Notice anything different? No? Of course not. Because they’re exaclty the same. Well, except for one’s better defined than the other but I just assume that’s Adam’s art evolving. Still pretty interesting, right?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
