        "raw": "<p>Okay, so I&rsquo;m sure several, if not all of you, have the foil cards. And I&rsquo;m assuming most of you are eagle eyed. So, I was wondering if you noticed a peculiar thing about Mr. Fixer&rsquo;s incap, both foil and regular.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here&rsquo;s mr. fixer&rsquo;s incap</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://greaterthangames.com/system/files/forum/attachments/72666623-50B2-43A8-8286-0AFA11AF0599.jpeg\" style=\"width: 278px; height: 360px;\" /></p><p>And here&rsquo;s his foil incap</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://greaterthangames.com/system/files/forum/attachments/3277740E-B1BB-49C6-BDEB-6D8A42D8E30D.png\" style=\"width: 252px; height: 360px;\" /></p><p>Notice anything different? No? Of course not. Because they&rsquo;re exaclty the same. Well, except for one&rsquo;s better defined than the other but I just assume that&rsquo;s Adam&rsquo;s art evolving. Still pretty interesting, right?</p>",
