        "raw": "[quote=\"X-metal\"]\n\nunrelated: what dies the writing in the incap say?\n\n[/quote]\n\nFrom this post&nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/50041#comment-50041\">https://greaterthangames.com/comment/50041#comment-50041</a>\n\n[quote=\"dpt\"]\n\nI&#39;m not really competent, but I answered it here:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/36658#comment-36658\">https://greaterthangames.com/comment/36658#comment-36658</a>. The top does read &quot;Owari&quot;, The End, as you gussed. (I&#39;m not clear how much this implies he is actually dead.)I missed the other block. That is a signature block, and is written in katakana, one of the Japanese phonetic syllabries, the one typically used for foreign words. It reads &quot;Adamu Rebotaro&quot;, i.e., Adam&nbsp;Rebottaro.In addition to his Nemesis symbol (to fix/mend), the other Kanji I noticed on his cards is on the style cards; I believe they are names of the relevant animal in Japanese, although I haven&#39;t checked carefully.\n\n[/quote]\n\n",
