        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I recall Christopher saying at some point that if we ever see Mr Fixer without his hat, it means he's dead. That's why Dark Watch Fixer has no hat - he's some kind of sentient zombie version that got brought back by Zhu Long and the other members of the Dark Watch had to fight him at first or something because he didn't remember himself/them. May have been under Zhu Long's control in some way, I'm not sure. Anyway, Zhu Long seems to give people dragon tattoos when he rezzes them, because the same thing happened to the Operative.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>well, yeah. Fixer - hat = dead but that still doesn’t explain why the incap art is the same.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
